#@upstream=dcm-client
#@dest=.
# card-platform twin manifest (master: general-manager/docs/twin/client.exclude) — the per-app paths of a dcm-client twin
# (one twin repo per store app: batak-client, basra-client …). Everything not listed here is overwritten by
# twin/sync-upstream.sh. Never edit a synced path on a twin: change dcm-client and re-sync. A twin-only file must live
# under one of these paths. rsync patterns, anchored at the dcm-client root. Folder lines need their .meta twin.
# Drafted before P1c (client AppCore extraction); P1c finalises the Addressables and Editor lines.

# the game folder: Crossle's is not copied; add the twin's own below it (never deleted)
/Assets/DontCrossMe
/Assets/DontCrossMe.meta
# twin game folder — the twin writes its own lines, e.g. batak-client /Assets/Batak, basra-client /Assets/Basra (+ .meta):
#/Assets/<Game>
#/Assets/<Game>.meta

# the twin's own socket DTOs, exported by its game server (card-backend/game-server/Tools/generate-socket-shared.sh
# --game=<G> --client-dir=…): SocketShared/Game/<G> is not in dcm-client, so it must be protected from --delete — the twin
# writes its own lines (batak-client Game/Batak, basra-client Game/Basra, + .meta)
#/Assets/SharedData/SocketShared/Game/<G>
#/Assets/SharedData/SocketShared/Game/<G>.meta

# per-app assets that shared scenes/prefabs reference by GUID (item icons, reward view database, splash + booster art):
# a twin ships its own files with the same GUIDs (card-platform P1c, dcm-client Docs/AI_RULES.md)
/Assets/AppData
/Assets/AppData.meta

# per-game art swap (2026-11-26): the twin's copy of these images carries the upstream GUID (heart icons in
# Assets/GameComponents/Heart/Sprites/, splash in Assets/AppData/Art/), so the shared copy must not exist in the twin —
# two files with one GUID make Unity give the shared copy a new GUID, which --check reports as drift
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Icon/ui_icon_heart.png
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Icon/ui_icon_heart.png.meta
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Icon/ui_icon_heart_broken.png
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Icon/ui_icon_heart_broken.png.meta
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Icon/ui_icon_heart_unlimited.png
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Icon/ui_icon_heart_unlimited.png.meta
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Splash/splash.png
/Assets/GameComponents/Core/Sprites/Splash/splash.png.meta
# the twin's heart icons (same GUIDs as dcm-client's Core/Sprites/Icon copies). dcm-client's Heart/Sprites holds only an
# Editor~ folder; the folder's .meta stays synced, its contents are the twin's own
/Assets/GameComponents/Heart/Sprites/*

# app identity, servers, store catalog, build stamp
/Assets/Resources/AppConfig*.json
/Assets/Resources/AppConfig*.json.meta
/Assets/Resources/IAPProductCatalog.json
/Assets/Resources/IAPProductCatalog.json.meta
/Assets/Resources/buildInfo.json
/Assets/Resources/buildInfo.json.meta
/ProjectSettings/ProjectSettings.asset
/ProjectSettings/EditorBuildSettings.asset
/user_keystores/

# Firebase / Google services are per app id
/Assets/google-services.json
/Assets/google-services.json.meta
/Assets/GoogleService-Info.plist
/Assets/GoogleService-Info.plist.meta
/Assets/StreamingAssets/google-services-desktop.json
/Assets/StreamingAssets/google-services-desktop.json.meta
/Assets/GeneratedLocalRepo
/Assets/GeneratedLocalRepo.meta
/ProjectSettings/AndroidResolverDependencies.xml

# Addressables: group list + content state are per app until P1c splits shared vs game groups
/Assets/AddressableAssetsData/AddressableAssetSettings.asset
/Assets/AddressableAssetsData/AssetGroups/
/Assets/AddressableAssetsData/Android/
/Assets/AddressableAssetsData/Windows/

# stray files tracked by dcm-client that no twin wants
/fbg.log
/mono_crash.mem.*
